rticle that  is not in the standard model which  generates  generates this additional gravitational  pull that's what's called dark matter  dark because uh we can't actually see it  we only notice its gravitational  attraction the other possibility is that  uh there's something about gravity that  we just don't  understand and this goes under the name  modified gravity  either way there's something about the  foundations  of physics that needs to change to  explain these observations and then  there are other questions like how did  the universe begin what's with the  measurement  process and quantum mechanics and so on  and so that they're good  reasons to think that um we have not  found what's ultimately the correct  description  of nature and yes these  are hard questions uh physics is a very  mature discipline  it's one of the oldest scientists that  there is and the  simple things have been done so you  expect some kind of slowdown for example  because it becomes  more and more difficult to make  experiments  that probe areas where we have not  already found out everything that there  was uh to  be found out this is why we see larger  and larger experiments larger and larger  collaborations  uh more and more expensive experiments  um of course  but the main reason for the slowdown is  not  this difficulty because we still make  these experiments  um and um we still see a lot of  theoretical  activity in these areas it's just that  it doesn't seem to be going anywhere  it's like people are running faster and  faster but they're running on a  treadmill not getting  anywhere so what's really the cause of  the problem  is bad methodology and group think  what's what's really um at the core of  the problem is that physicists and  foundations of physics  rely on beauty to discover the next  best fundamental law they  think that the foundations of physics  the way that we currently have them  as as with general relativity and the  standard model are just not  pretty 