  begin with then you go test them you get  negative experimental results so  negative experimental results are also  results of course but they're not very  useful results if you want to construct  a new theory so you get this lack of  data  and you get stuck with the unpromising  theories and  um this creates a vicious cycle that um  physicists have been in um for 40 years  basically  so um what's my progress proposal well  uh if you look at the history of physics  uh you will find  that um whenever there was a progress  led by theory of course there has been  progress led by experiment  but i'm i'm talking about progress by  theoretical predictions  this was led by resolving real  inconsistencies  in the theories so i suggest that before  physicists try to solve a problem they  make sure  it really is a problem and just because  the theory is not as beautiful as you  would like it to be  that doesn't mean the theory has a  problem it's really uh mathematical  problems that you need to be able to  um formally uh write down whose solution  has led to progress uh in the past  and so it makes sense just looking at  the evidence the historical evidence uh  to try and do that  again so what are those real problems uh  that we currently have on the  foundations of physics  well i already mentioned them in the  very beginning  we have this lack of a theory of quantum  gravity that's a case of an  actual inconsistency in the mathematics  we have the quantum measurement problem  that too is just a mathematical  inconsistency that  requires a solution we have dark matter  so this is not an internal inconsistency  in the theory but it's an actual  inconsistency with observation  so this two requires a solution  and there are certain aspects of dark  energy that are also inconsistencies  um but not all of them in particular  just the smallness of the cosmological  constant  is not in and by itself uh an  inconsistency  so this brings me to my summary uh using  criteria of beauty to assess theories  is bad scientific methodology it has not  worked  for 40 years to rely on arguments from  beauty  and continuing to insist that that's the  way to go  it's just not good science physicist  should stop doing this  there is no reason to think that it  should work it has not worked and it  does not currently work  and that's just not the way forward  finally allow me to say that i have  written a book in which i have  fleshed out these arguments some more  which will be published as a paperback  in about  10 days thank you for your attention for  more debates  talks and interviews subscribe today to  the institute  of art and ideas at iai tv  you

